'''GWizard Citation Fix''' is a third-party [[Addons|addon]] that <one-sentence summary of the genealogical problem it solves>.

[[File:gwizard_citationfix-main.png|thumb|right|350px|GWizard Citation Fix main interface]]

== Overview ==

'''GWizard Citation Fix''' provides review steps for cleaning citation-related data in the active Family Tree. You can inspect suggested changes for sources, repositories, citations, citation attributes, citation media, and notes before applying them. The tool can also create a citation analysis report or run all cleanup steps without reviewing each set of hints.

== Usage ==

# In Gramps, open '''Tools > Family Tree Processing > GWizard Citation Fix'''. '''[VERIFY MENU PATH]'''
# In the '''GWizard Citation Fix''' window, choose a button below to open its report or cleanup step.
# Review the suggestions in a cleanup dialog and use '''Apply''' to apply its changes. To run steps without reviewing them individually, use '''Accept all hints'''.
# Close the open window or dialog when you are finished.

Main-window buttons, in screen order:

* '''Generate report''' — choose a file for the citation analysis report; the saved report then opens in a report window.
* '''Unpack Conflated Source''' — review suggestions to unpack mixed source text and prepare source fields.
* '''Repository Consolidate''' — review suggestions for consolidating repositories.
* '''Fix Repositories''' — review suggestions to create missing repositories and link sources to repositories.
* '''Fix Sources''' — review suggestions to merge near-duplicate sources and quarantine non-sources.
* '''Unpack Conflated Citation''' — review suggestions to extract dates and URLs from citation fields or notes.
* '''Fix Citations''' — review suggested citation page, date, and confidence cleanup.
* '''Citation Attributes''' — review suggested GPS quality attributes and confidence ratings.
* '''Link Citation Media''' — review suggestions for linking media to citations.
* '''Fix Notes''' — review suggested cleanup of citation notes.
* '''Accept all hints''' — confirm and run the cleanup steps without reviewing each step's hints.

=== Generate report ===

# Click '''Generate report'''. The '''Save Citation Fix Report''' file chooser opens.
   [[File:gwizard_citationfix-generate-report-save.png|thumb|The Save Citation Fix Report file chooser with the report filename]]
# Choose a location and file name. The default name is <code>CitationFixReport.txt</code>. Click '''Save'''.
# When the report has been written, the '''GWizard Citation Fix report''' window opens with its contents.
   [[File:gwizard_citationfix-generate-report.png|thumb|The GWizard Citation Fix report window displaying the generated report]]
# Click '''Close''' to return to the main window.

=== Unpack Conflated Source ===

# Click '''Unpack Conflated Source'''. The '''Unpack Conflated Source''' dialog opens.
   [[File:gwizard_citationfix-unpack-conflated-source.png|thumb|The Unpack Conflated Source dialog showing source-field suggestions]]
# Review the suggested changes for mixed source text, repository entries, and publication information.
# Click '''Apply''' to apply the selected changes, or '''Close''' to leave the dialog.

=== Repository Consolidate ===

# Click '''Repository Consolidate'''. The '''Repository Consolidate''' dialog opens.
   [[File:gwizard_citationfix-repository-consolidate.png|thumb|The Repository Consolidate dialog showing repositories to consolidate]]
# Review the repository suggestions and select the intended target where needed.
# Click '''Apply''' to apply the changes, or '''Close''' to leave the dialog.

=== Fix Repositories ===

# Click '''Fix Repositories'''. The '''Fix Repositories''' dialog opens.
   [[File:gwizard_citationfix-fix-repositories.png|thumb|The Fix Repositories dialog showing source and repository suggestions]]
# Review the suggested repository links and any missing repository entries.
# Click '''Apply''' to apply the changes, or '''Close''' to leave the dialog.

=== Fix Sources ===

# Click '''Fix Sources'''. The '''Fix Sources''' dialog opens.
   [[File:gwizard_citationfix-fix-sources.png|thumb|The Fix Sources dialog showing source cleanup suggestions]]
# Review the suggested source merges and any entries identified as non-sources.
# Click '''Apply''' to apply the changes, or '''Close''' to leave the dialog.

=== Unpack Conflated Citation ===

# Click '''Unpack Conflated Citation'''. The '''Unpack Conflated Citation''' dialog opens.
   [[File:gwizard_citationfix-unpack-conflated-citation.png|thumb|The Unpack Conflated Citation dialog showing citation-field suggestions]]
# Review the suggestions for extracting dates and URLs from volume/page fields or notes.
# Click '''Apply''' to apply the changes, or '''Close''' to leave the dialog.

=== Fix Citations ===

# Click '''Fix Citations'''. The '''Fix Citations''' dialog opens.
   [[File:gwizard_citationfix-fix-citations.png|thumb|The Fix Citations dialog showing page, date, and confidence suggestions]]
# Review the suggested cleanup for citation page, date, and confidence values.
# Click '''Apply''' to apply the changes, or '''Close''' to leave the dialog.

=== Citation Attributes ===

# Click '''Citation Attributes'''. The '''Citation Attributes''' dialog opens.
   [[File:gwizard_citationfix-citation-attributes.png|thumb|The Citation Attributes dialog showing suggested citation attributes]]
# Review the suggested Genealogical Proof Standard (GPS) attributes—Source Type, Information Type, and Evidence Type—and confidence ratings.
# Click '''Apply''' to apply the changes, or '''Close''' to leave the dialog.

=== Link Citation Media ===

# Click '''Link Citation Media'''. The '''Link Citation Media''' dialog opens.
   [[File:gwizard_citationfix-link-citation-media.png|thumb|The Link Citation Media dialog showing media-to-citation link suggestions]]
# Review the proposed media links. Select a row and click '''Inspect''' to examine that link in the inspector.
# Click '''Apply''' to apply the selected links, or '''Close''' to leave the dialog.

=== Fix Notes ===

# Click '''Fix Notes'''. The '''Fix Notes''' dialog opens.
   [[File:gwizard_citationfix-fix-notes.png|thumb|The Fix Notes dialog showing citation notes for review]]
# Review the notes suggested for cleanup.
# Click '''Apply''' to apply the changes, or '''Close''' to leave the dialog.

=== Accept all hints ===

# Click '''Accept all hints'''. The '''Accept all hints''' confirmation dialog explains that the steps will run without individual review.
   [[File:gwizard_citationfix-accept-all-hints.png|thumb|The Accept all hints confirmation dialog]]
# Click '''Accept all''' to proceed, or '''Cancel''' to return to the main window.
# After the run, the '''Accept All Hints Complete''' window shows the results and any changes requiring human intervention.
   [[File:gwizard_citationfix-accept-all-hints-complete.png|thumb|The Accept All Hints Complete window showing the run results]]
# Click '''Close''' to return to the main window.

== Configure Options ==

* The main window has no configurable options such as checkboxes, fields, or preferences.

== Features ==

* Reviews cleanup suggestions for source titles and fields, repositories, sources, citation fields, citation attributes, citation media, and notes.
* Provides an individual review dialog for each cleanup step, with '''Apply''' and '''Close''' controls.
* Generates a citation analysis report at a location and file name you choose, then displays the saved report.
* '''Accept all hints''' runs the cleanup steps without individual review and displays a results window, including items that need human intervention.
